First Author: Noh
Title: Machine Learning for 1-Year Graft Failure Prediction in Lung Transplant Recipients: The Korean Organ Transplantation Registry
Source number: 68

Very short summary: This prospective multicenter registry study included 240 South Korean lung transplant recipients enrolled between 2015 and 2021. Six machine-learning models were evaluated using stratified 5-fold cross-validation; the nine-variable multilayer perceptron achieved the best performance for 1-year graft failure, with an AUC of 0.780, accuracy of 73.3%, sensitivity of 67.3%, and specificity of 75.1%.

